# What Cloudflare is allowed to publish. Read this before adding a root-level file.
#
# The assets directory is the repo root, and wrangler does NOT read .gitignore --
# it uploads every file it finds. So this is an ALLOW-LIST, not a deny-list:
# ignore everything at the root, then re-admit only the site itself.
#
# Failure mode of an allow-list is a missing file (loud). Failure mode of a
# deny-list is publishing cookies.txt to the public internet (silent). Hence this.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore's, and `/*` only matches top-level entries, so re-admitting
# a directory re-admits everything under it.

/*

!/index.html
!/styles.css
!/css
!/js
!/assets

# Inter and Roboto Mono are self-hosted in every target. Keeping `fonts/`
# admitted makes the browser and native package use the same typography without
# a third-party request or offline fallback.
!/fonts

# `_headers` deliberately stays OUT of the allow-list. Wrangler still reads it from
# the assets directory and applies its rules at the edge; listing it here only stops
# it being served as a downloadable file. (Same pattern as the Pages migration docs.)

# Belt and braces. These are listed again, after the negations, so that a careless
# edit above still cannot publish them.
cookies.txt
.git
.github
.wrangler
.dev.vars
node_modules

# Native packaging + local toolchain. All top-level, so the `/*` rule above already
# excludes them; repeated here because the cost of being wrong is publishing a JDK,
# an Android SDK and a signed APK to the public edge. `.toolchain/` alone is ~6.5 GB.
.toolchain
android
ios
www
resources
icons
scripts
tools
*.apk
*.aab
